g. The network correctly labels this substitution as hypothetical. Subsequent aldehyde trapping and homologation follow the stronger scaffold, but cannot compensate for an unvalidated entry reduction. This is not a wholly copper-free pathway because rxn_001 still requires Cu(I). Acidic endpoint recovery is also unresolved.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_006\",\n        \"rxn_017\",\n        \"rxn_018\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Compare copper-assisted and copper-free rxn_006 conditions at matched spectral irradiance, sulfur concentration, and pH.\",\n        \"Measure aldehyde capture versus decomposition or cyclization, including effects of residual copper from rxn_001 and dissolved iron.\",\n        \"Demonstrate free-arginine production after the proposed acidic processing.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P4\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_001\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_002\": 0.92,\n        \"rxn_003\": 0.76,\n        \"rxn_007\": 0.56,\n        \"rxn_011\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_012\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_013\": 0.87,\n        \"rxn_014\": 0.85,\n        \"rxn_015\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_016\": 0.88,\n        \"rxn_017\": 0.8,\n        \"rxn_018\": 0.82\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.72,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.83,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.58,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.56,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.67,\n      \"feedback\": \"This pathway combines inefficient early guanidination with an unvalidated copper-free reduction of the guanidinated nitrile. General evidence for sulfide photoreduction does not establish the substrate-specific behavior of mol_013, including its protonation, competing reactions, and productive hemiaminal formation. The later transformations remain chemically coherent, but the pathway lacks evidence that sufficient material reaches them. Free arginine is still an expected rather than demonstrated endpoint under the stated conditions.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_003\",\n        \"rxn_007\",\n        \"rxn_017\",\n        \"rxn_018\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Test rxn_007 using authenticated mol_013 and appropriate dark, sulfur-free, and copper-assisted controls.\",\n        \"Distinguish genuine copper-free activity from residual copper carried over from rxn_001.\",\n        \"Quantify the early-guanidination material balance and subsequent acidic arginine recovery.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P5\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_001\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_002\": 0.92,\n        \"rxn_008\": 0.58,\n        \"rxn_010\": 0.93,\n        \"rxn_011\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_012\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_013\": 0.87,\n        \"rxn_014\": 0.85,\n        \"rxn_015\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_016\": 0.88,\n        \"rxn_017\": 0.8,\n        \"rxn_018\": 0.82\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.75,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.85,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.59,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.58,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.69,\n      \"feedback\": \"Ranjan et al. (2018) support the potential environmental availability of sulfite, but do not establish rxn_008 on this substrate. Its balanced redox equation is necessary but insufficient evidence for useful photochemical conversion. Sulfite/bisulfite interactions with the generated aldehyde may also affect cyanamide trapping. This substitution does not eliminate the reduced-sulfur requirements of the later thioamide chemistry. The final acidic hydrolysis sequence remains unquantified.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_008\",\n        \"rxn_017\",\n        \"rxn_018\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Measure the action spectrum, aldehyde yield, and competing products of rxn_008 under specified sulfite speciation and pH.\",\n        \"Test whether sulfite/bisulfite carbonyl adducts interfere with rxn_010.\",\n        \"Specify reduced-sulfur delivery for downstream reactions and validate free-arginine recovery after hydrolysis.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P6\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_001\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_002\": 0.92,\n        \"rxn_003\": 0.76,\n        \"rxn_009\": 0.54,\n        \"rxn_011\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_012\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_013\": 0.87,\n        \"rxn_014\": 0.85,\n        \"rxn_015\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_016\": 0.88,\n        \"rxn_017\": 0.8,\n        \"rxn_018\": 0.82\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.71,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.82,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.57,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.55,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.66,\n      \"feedback\": \"The conserved stoichiometry of rxn_009 does not validate sulfite-driven reduction of the early-guanylated nitrile. This substrate-specific substitution is unsupported by the supplied experimental findings and follows an already inefficient guanidination step. The environmental motivation for sulfite is reasonable, but successful reduction, hemiaminal formation, and compatibility with subsequent sulfide chemistry remain hypotheses. The pathway correctly avoids claiming that sulfite replaces sulfur incorporation throughout the network.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_003\",\n        \"rxn_009\",\n        \"rxn_017\",\n        \"rxn_018\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Establish rxn_009 conversion and selectivity with authenticated mol_013 rather than extrapolating from unrelated sulfite photoreductions.\",\n        \"Quantify early guanidination and test transfer from sulfite-containing mixtures into the downstream sulfide chemistry.\",\n        \"Demonstrate the acidic endpoint with an arginine-specific product balance.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P7