entration.\",\n        \"Measure residual copper and organic-material recovery after any proposed precipitation, sorption, or separation step.\",\n        \"Determine whether aldehyde production and immediate cyanamide capture outcompete substrate and reagent losses.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P4\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_001\": 0.88,\n        \"rxn_002\": 0.92,\n        \"rxn_005\": 0.68,\n        \"rxn_008\": 0.54,\n        \"rxn_009\": 0.87,\n        \"rxn_010\": 0.88,\n        \"rxn_011\": 0.84,\n        \"rxn_012\": 0.81,\n        \"rxn_013\": 0.88,\n        \"rxn_014\": 0.88,\n        \"rxn_015\": 0.8,\n        \"rxn_016\": 0.75\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.7,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.77,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.51,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.57,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.64,\n      \"feedback\": \"This variant combines inefficient early guanidination with an unestablished copper-free reduction of the guanidinated nitrile. General sulfide photoreactivity cannot substitute for evidence that mol_011 forms the intended aldehyde/hemiaminal selectively. The subsequent homologation sequence is coherent, and all reactions pass the supplied conservation check, but productive flux through the first two distinguishing steps is uncertain. Acidic finishing adds the same unresolved endpoint as P1.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_005\",\n        \"rxn_008\",\n        \"rxn_015\",\n        \"rxn_016\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Test authenticated mol_011 directly under copper-depleted irradiation conditions and identify the product distribution.\",\n        \"Quantify early guanidination before attempting an integrated sequence, including the contribution of residual cyanamide to alternative productive chemistry.\",\n        \"Demonstrate copper depletion without assuming quantitative retention of the organic 